  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674384",
      "title": "Remix vs NextJS",
      "lectureOrder": 3,
      "videoOrder": 3,
      "sourceHash": "572f40a02c3640c0cf793309f7c518ae1452efdf86b3410b391d64f721d8ae9e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "Now in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "you learned what Remix is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 6.78,
          "en": "and why you might want to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.78,
          "end": 9.99,
          "en": "Now, maybe what you learned there sounds familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.99,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "There is another framework for React called Next JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 17.07,
          "en": "which kind of aims to solve the same problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.07,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "which also helps with building full stack applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 24.54,
          "en": "And indeed, I do have a full course about Next JS as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 26.52,
          "en": "But there are some important differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.52,
          "end": 29.1,
          "en": "between Remix and Next JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "For example, with Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "you always render all pages on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "So whenever a user enters a URL leading to your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "that page that's being served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "is rendered on the server, on the fly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 45.03,
          "en": "So the user always gets the latest data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.03,
          "end": 46.56,
          "en": "and a brand new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.56,
          "end": 49.02,
          "en": "Of course, you can set up some caching if you want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "but generally it is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 53.1,
          "en": "when a user visits the site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.1,
          "end": 54.3,
          "en": "With Next JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.3,
          "end": 57.33,
          "en": "you can write some code that forces a page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.33,
          "end": 58.931,
          "en": "to be rendered for every request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.931,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "but that's just optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 63.45,
          "en": "because in most cases you write code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.45,
          "end": 67.2,
          "en": "where the site is statically generated at built time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.2,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "So right before deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 72.87,
          "en": "With Remix, this is not supported with Next JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.87,
          "end": 76.833,
          "en": "It's basically the standard or the default for many pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.82,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "Therefore, for Remix,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "if you wanna deploy it, you always need a host,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "a server that supports server side code execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "With Next JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "that's not necessarily the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 92.096,
          "en": "because there if you pre-rendered all pages at build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.096,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "you only need a static host.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.50999999999999,
          "en": "You only need a host that's capable of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.50999999999999,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "server side code execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "For Next JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 101.13,
          "en": "if you're using this optional feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 101.13,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "of rendering certain pages on the server, on the fly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 106.789,
          "en": "But these are just some technical differences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 106.789,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "There also are many syntax differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "and even though I really like Next JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 111.84,
          "end": 113.691,
          "en": "and it is absolutely amazing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 113.691,
          "end": 116.369,
          "en": "I think that Remix has an even nicer API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 116.369,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "and that that building Remix apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "is even more fun than it is to build next JS apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 123.459,
          "en": "which still is awesome, don't get me wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 123.459,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "but Remix is maybe more awesome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 128.523,
          "en": "We'll see after taking this course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
